        <item>
            <title>Siloquy 0.11.0</title>
            <pubDate>Fri, 26 Jun 2026 21:46:44 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.11.0</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.11.0</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
    <style>
      body { background:#fff; color:#1d1d1f; margin:0; padding:14px 16px;
             font:13px/1.5 -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif; }
      h2 { font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#0a84ff; margin:0 0 .4em; }
      h3 { font-size:.8em; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase;
           letter-spacing:.05em; color:#86868b; margin:1.1em 0 .35em; }
      ul { margin:.2em 0 .9em; padding-left:1.25em; }
      li { margin:.35em 0; }
      code { font-family:ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace; font-size:.88em;
             background:#f0f0f2; padding:.08em .35em; border-radius:4px; }
    </style>
    <h2>0.11.0</h2>
    <h3>Added</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Recommended settings: onboarding now ends with a &quot;One last thing&quot; step that applies a set of sensible defaults in one click, and Settings → General has a new &quot;Recommended Settings…&quot; button that does the same any time. The default enhancement model is unchanged.</li>
      <li>The onboarding Keyboard Shortcuts step now also sets up the enhancement toggle, pre-assigned to Right Option (⌥). You still choose your own recording shortcut, and you can change or clear the enhancement shortcut.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Fixed</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>On a fresh install, the Screen Recording onboarding step no longer opens System Settings at the same moment macOS shows its own permission dialog — the two were racing and left the dialog stuck. The dialog now appears on its own the first time; later attempts open System Settings instead.</li>
    </ul>
            ]]></description>
