            <title>Siloquy 0.10.4</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 23 Jun 2026 11:10:37 +0000</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>0.10.4</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>0.10.4</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description><![CDATA[
    <style>
      body { background:#fff; color:#1d1d1f; margin:0; padding:14px 16px;
             font:13px/1.5 -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif; }
      h2 { font-size:1.6em; font-weight:700; color:#0a84ff; margin:0 0 .4em; }
      h3 { font-size:.8em; font-weight:700; text-transform:uppercase;
           letter-spacing:.05em; color:#86868b; margin:1.1em 0 .35em; }
      ul { margin:.2em 0 .9em; padding-left:1.25em; }
      li { margin:.35em 0; }
      code { font-family:ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace; font-size:.88em;
             background:#f0f0f2; padding:.08em .35em; border-radius:4px; }
    </style>
    <h2>0.10.4</h2>
    <h3>Fixed</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>iCloud sync of your dictionary (word replacements and custom vocabulary) across machines now works. v0.10.3 declared the iCloud entitlements but was missing <code>com.apple.application-identifier</code>, so CloudKit couldn&#x27;t initialise the container and sync never started; this adds it.</li>
      <li>The in-app update window now shows clean, formatted release notes instead of rendering the GitHub release web page.</li>
    </ul>
            ]]></description>
